       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe and may be a mistake.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Each dose is 1600 mg.** The usual maximum single dose of oral ibuprofen is 800 mg, so this is twice that.\n- **The daily total would be 6400 mg** (1600 mg \u00d7 4). The usual maximum for prescriptions is 3200 mg/day, so this is twice that too. A dose this high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and other toxicity, especially in a 70-year-old.\n\n**Was one of these intended?**\n1. **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). This is a common mix-up between the per-dose and daily amounts.\n2. **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum).\n3. **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2400 mg/day), or some other regimen.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do mean 1600 mg QID, please confirm and give the clinical reason. I'll put that reason in the order note so pharmacy can see it when they review the order."
      }
